[ system ]
    A player rated an output of a task in a Skyrim game as weak or bad and said why. The game uses this output itself; it is not a line someone speaks. You see the task, the scene, that output, what the player found wrong with it, and a new output for the same moment. Decide whether the new output still has those problems.
    Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: {"still_has_problem": true|false, "reason": "<one sentence>"}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    <task>{{ judge_task.template }}</task>
    <scene>
    [ raw ]
{{ render_template("eval\\judge_scene") }}
    [ end raw ]
    </scene>
    <flagged_output>
    [ raw ]
{{ flagged_reply }}
    [ end raw ]
    </flagged_output>
    <problem>
    The player rated it {{ flagged_rating }} of 5 ({% if flagged_rating <= 1 %}broken{% else if flagged_rating == 2 %}bad{% else %}weak{% endif %}).
{% if length(tag_list) > 0 %}
    What was wrong:
{{ render_template("eval\\tag_list") }}
{% else %}
    The player did not say what was wrong.
{% endif %}
{% if length(flagged_note) > 0 %}
    The player's words: {{ flagged_note }}
{% endif %}
    </problem>
    <new_output>
    [ raw ]
{{ new_reply }}
    [ end raw ]
    </new_output>
[ end user ]
